  <p>
    vis-a-vis verification is a video installation exploring reflection,
    repetition, bodily presence and the unstable relationship between an image
    and its counterpart.
  </p>

  <p>
    Through mirrored movements and fragmented visual sequences, the work
    examines how recognition is produced between two opposing images and how
    that recognition can gradually become uncertain.
